WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.673 --> 00:00:03.791
- [Narrator] This a male tree pangolin.

00:00:03.791 --> 00:00:05.541
He is six months old.

00:00:10.363 --> 00:00:12.485
Critically endangered
and under-researched,

00:00:12.485 --> 00:00:16.752
the tree pangolin is a
mammalian species like no other.

00:00:16.752 --> 00:00:18.425
Found throughout Asia and Africa,

00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:21.793
pangolins can be traced
back 66 million years,

00:00:21.793 --> 00:00:24.637
meaning they lived amongst dinosaurs.

00:00:24.637 --> 00:00:27.622
They're the only mammals
on Earth covered in scales,

00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:31.440
which account for about
20% of their body weight.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.628
These large, protective
scales are made of keratin,

00:00:34.628 --> 00:00:38.729
the same thing human nails
and hair are made from.

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:40.620
Tree pangolins use their long claws

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.399
to climb on trees and branches

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:44.650
in an endless search for prey.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.900
Baby pangolins, like the one here,

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.706
get around by riding their mother's tails.

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:51.835
Though they have poor
eyesight and hearing,

00:00:51.835 --> 00:00:54.622
their strong sense of
smell and elastic tongue

00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:59.018
allows them to catch a meal
of mostly ants and termites.

00:00:59.018 --> 00:01:00.545
When the pangolin senses danger,

00:01:00.545 --> 00:01:02.308
it will curl up into a ball,

00:01:02.308 --> 00:01:05.136
making it almost invincible in the wild.

00:01:05.136 --> 00:01:08.918
Humans, however, are a dangerous threat.

00:01:08.918 --> 00:01:11.776
The pangolin scales are thought
to have healing properties,

00:01:11.776 --> 00:01:14.530
though there's no science to back that up.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:15.450
Because of that,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.592
pangolins are the most
heavily trafficked mammals

00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:19.049
in the world,

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.389
worth almost $300 per
pound on the black market.

00:01:23.389 --> 00:01:26.136
No one knows how many pangolins are left,

00:01:26.136 --> 00:01:30.354
but we do know that their
number is shrinking fast.

00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:32.604
This is the tree pangolin.

